    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "title": "Quiz: The Four Perception Moves",
     "question": "Which sequence correctly orders the four moves of Stoic perception as taught in Part I?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Alter perspective → control emotion → see clearly → practice objectivity",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "See clearly → control emotion → practice objectivity → alter perspective",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Practice objectivity → alter perspective → see clearly → control emotion",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Control emotion → alter perspective → practice objectivity → see clearly",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The order is **operational**. You cannot control emotion until you've stripped the narrative (see clearly). You cannot practice objectivity (view from outside) until your emotion is no longer running the show. And only after you've achieved objectivity can you choose a legitimate alternative frame. Holiday's sequencing matches the Stoic action chain in Marcus's Meditations: *perceive → judge → act*. Reversing the order means you reframe while still inside the emotional surge — that produces denial, not perception.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Knowledge Check</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Order matters</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\">Step 1: See Clearly</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Strip event from narrative.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"360\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\">Step 2: Control Emotion</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"475\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Name. Delay. Test for usefulness.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\">Step 3: Practice Objectivity</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"655\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Third-person. Time zoom. Stakes zoom.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"720\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\">Step 4: Alter Perspective</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"835\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Reframe. Apply both legitimacy tests.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Operational sequence: perceive, judge, act."
     }
    }
