     "explanation": "The right answer **integrates all three simultaneously**, exactly as the capstone teaches. Perception keeps her honest about what is actually happening (one rejection ≠ round failure). Action keeps her shipping (next 5 conversations scheduled, pitch iterated). Will keeps her sustainable (clear sorting of what's hers, premeditation for likely no's, service framing of the work for customers). Single-discipline approaches collapse: perception-only sees clearly but doesn't ship; action-only burns out; will-only endures but doesn't move. The Stoic operator runs all three on the same obstacle in parallel. This is Marcus on the Danube, Lincoln in 1862, Saban in any quarter, Stockdale in Hỏa Lò. Same engine. Different hardware.",
